## Original Content
From McDonald's to Wendy's, longtime Coke customers have been expanding their beverage offerings to boost their profit margins.

## Summary
Coca-Cola operates secretive innovation labs working on automating the preparation of specialty beverages like 'dirty soda' and refreshers. Meanwhile, longtime customers such as McDonald's and Wendy's have been expanding their beverage offerings as a strategy to improve profit margins.

## Key Points
- Coca-Cola maintains secretive innovation labs dedicated to beverage development and automation
- The company is pursuing automation technology for making 'dirty soda' and refresher drinks
- McDonald's and Wendy's are longstanding Coca-Cola customers expanding their beverage menus
- Restaurant chains view expanded beverage offerings as a way to boost profit margins


